/E (Quantization is the process of reducing the precision of the weights or activations in a neural network model. This technique is mainly used to make models smaller, faster, and more efficient, the model's parameters \(weights\) are often stored as 32-bit floating-point numbers \(FP32\). Quantization reduces the precision of these values, using lower-bit representations like 8-bit integers \(INT8\) or 16-bit floating-point \(FP16\).)
